{"id":89,"date":"2016-10-08T17:51:53","date_gmt":"2016-10-08T17:51:53","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/?p=89"},"modified":"2016-11-15T15:52:17","modified_gmt":"2016-11-15T15:52:17","slug":"budapest-hungary","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/travel-log\/budapest-hungary\/","title":{"rendered":"Budapest, Hungary"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Everyone learns in school about the First and Second World Wars but no one really tells us that what happened in the aftermath of those devastating events were just as bad on the contemporary population. In Budapest, you clearly witness those wounds, left for everyone to see and to learn from.<\/p>\n<h5>Disclaimer: The pictures are taken with my phone because it was said to be a rainy weekend.<\/h5>\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-24 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox-free fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-small fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-24\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:false},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4405.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Abandoned buildings turned into ad billboards often line the streets.\" data-attachment-id=\"33\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Abandoned buildings turned into ad billboards often line the streets.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4405\/4000532017.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Abandoned buildings turned into ad billboards often line the streets.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4378.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The House of Terror, located on 60 Andr\u00e1ssy Boulevard, was first the headquarters of the Arrow Cross Party and then the political police (which had three forms: Department of Political Police, State Security Office and finally, State Security Authority). The Party got its symbol from the Magyar tribes, just like the Nazis got their Swastika from the Aryans. Just like the Nazis, the Arrow Cross Party was highly nationalistic and xenophobic. While both the Nazis and the Arrow Cross Party were anti-Semitic, the Arrow Cross Party was also anti-German.  Many horrors were committed in this house, notably the thousands of tortures committed in its basement.\" data-attachment-id=\"28\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The House of Terror, located on 60 Andr\u00e1ssy Boulevard, was first the headquarters of the Arrow Cross Party and then the political police (which had three forms: Department of Political Police, State Security Office and finally, State Security Authority). The Party got its symbol from the Magyar tribes, just like the Nazis got their Swastika from the Aryans. Just like the Nazis, the Arrow Cross Party was highly nationalistic and xenophobic. While both the Nazis and the Arrow Cross Party were anti-Semitic, the Arrow Cross Party was also anti-German.  Many horrors were committed in this house, notably the thousands of tortures committed in its basement.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4378\/438158393.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The House of Terror, located on 60 Andr\u00e1ssy Boulevard, was first the headquarters of the Arrow Cross Party and then the political police (which had three forms: Department of Political Police, State Security Office and finally, State Security Authority). The Party got its symbol from the Magyar tribes, just like the Nazis got their Swastika from the Aryans. Just like the Nazis, the Arrow Cross Party was highly nationalistic and xenophobic. While both the Nazis and the Arrow Cross Party were anti-Semitic, the Arrow Cross Party was also anti-German.  Many horrors were committed in this house, notably the thousands of tortures committed in its basement.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4386.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In 1945, while the Hungarian people voted for a democratic government, the Allied Control Commission ordered that the interior ministry be placed under communist control. Thus, the Hungarian Communist Party had control of the sole government-controlled armed forces. With this political police, the Hungarian Communist Party managed to assassinate the democratic politicians in power. By 1949, Hungarians no longer had the freedom to choose their preferred candidate for office.\" data-attachment-id=\"31\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In 1945, while the Hungarian people voted for a democratic government, the Allied Control Commission ordered that the interior ministry be placed under communist control. Thus, the Hungarian Communist Party had control of the sole government-controlled armed forces. With this political police, the Hungarian Communist Party managed to assassinate the democratic politicians in power. By 1949, Hungarians no longer had the freedom to choose their preferred candidate for office.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4386\/4050736635.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In 1945, while the Hungarian people voted for a democratic government, the Allied Control Commission ordered that the interior ministry be placed under communist control. Thus, the Hungarian Communist Party had control of the sole government-controlled armed forces. With this political police, the Hungarian Communist Party managed to assassinate the democratic politicians in power. By 1949, Hungarians no longer had the freedom to choose their preferred candidate for office.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4384.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"When the Hungarian Communist Party was organized after the Red Army&#039;s arrival, they gained a vast number of their recruits from the Arrow Cross Party.\" data-attachment-id=\"30\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"When the Hungarian Communist Party was organized after the Red Army&#039;s arrival, they gained a vast number of their recruits from the Arrow Cross Party.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4384\/3608183842.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">When the Hungarian Communist Party was organized after the Red Army's arrival, they gained a vast number of their recruits from the Arrow Cross Party.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4380.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"There were many victims in World War II beyond the vast number of Jews that perished in the war and its aftermath. The Church was persecuted because of its power and wealth. The kulaks were regularly beaten to instill fear in the other farmers as well as to harass them off their farms. The political police had quotas of enemies of the state that they would have to deport each month. Once they had deported all of the Germans and the Hungarians with German-sounding names, they forced civilians to inform on their neighbors. Whether those individuals had actually committed the crime that they were accused of was irrelevant because the political police always managed to get a signed confession, after extensive torturing. Even leaders of these terror organizations were not safe; G\u00e1bor P\u00e9ter, who had denounced his Jewish religion and committed countless atrocities for the communist party as the political police leader, was also tortured and sentenced to life imprisonment in 1954 for being a Zionist. (However, he sentence was reduced and he was set free in 1959.)\" data-attachment-id=\"29\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"There were many victims in World War II beyond the vast number of Jews that perished in the war and its aftermath. The Church was persecuted because of its power and wealth. The kulaks were regularly beaten to instill fear in the other farmers as well as to harass them off their farms. The political police had quotas of enemies of the state that they would have to deport each month. Once they had deported all of the Germans and the Hungarians with German-sounding names, they forced civilians to inform on their neighbors. Whether those individuals had actually committed the crime that they were accused of was irrelevant because the political police always managed to get a signed confession, after extensive torturing. Even leaders of these terror organizations were not safe; G\u00e1bor P\u00e9ter, who had denounced his Jewish religion and committed countless atrocities for the communist party as the political police leader, was also tortured and sentenced to life imprisonment in 1954 for being a Zionist. (However, he sentence was reduced and he was set free in 1959.)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4380\/1912981241.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">There were many victims in World War II beyond the vast number of Jews that perished in the war and its aftermath. The Church was persecuted because of its power and wealth. The kulaks were regularly beaten to instill fear in the other farmers as well as to harass them off their farms. The political police had quotas of enemies of the state that they would have to deport each month. Once they had deported all of the Germans and the Hungarians with German-sounding names, they forced civilians to inform on their neighbors. Whether those individuals had actually committed the crime that they were accused of was irrelevant because the political police always managed to get a signed confession, after extensive torturing. Even leaders of these terror organizations were not safe; G\u00e1bor P\u00e9ter, who had denounced his Jewish religion and committed countless atrocities for the communist party as the political police leader, was also tortured and sentenced to life imprisonment in 1954 for being a Zionist. (However, he sentence was reduced and he was set free in 1959.)<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4364.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Shoes on the Danube Bank: &quot;To the memory of the victims shot into the Danube by Arrow Cross militiamen in 1944\u201345. Erected 16 April 2005.\u201d\" data-attachment-id=\"25\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Shoes on the Danube Bank: &quot;To the memory of the victims shot into the Danube by Arrow Cross militiamen in 1944\u201345. Erected 16 April 2005.\u201d\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4364\/3760977634.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Shoes on the Danube Bank: \"To the memory of the victims shot into the Danube by Arrow Cross militiamen in 1944\u201345. Erected 16 April 2005.\u201d<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4369.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Parliament: The Warsaw Pact was created on May 14th, 1955 in response to Western Germany&#039;s integration into NATO. On October 23rd, 1956, university students protested in front of Parliament. While there was no leader at the beginning, the revolt caught fire across Hungary. By the end of October, the violence had almost come to an end and the Soviets agreed to let Hungary out of the Warsaw Pact. On November 4th, however, the Politburo changed its mind and the Soviet Army crushed the revolt. The Revolution of 1856 was the first threat to Soviet control.\" data-attachment-id=\"26\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Parliament: The Warsaw Pact was created on May 14th, 1955 in response to Western Germany&#039;s integration into NATO. On October 23rd, 1956, university students protested in front of Parliament. While there was no leader at the beginning, the revolt caught fire across Hungary. By the end of October, the violence had almost come to an end and the Soviets agreed to let Hungary out of the Warsaw Pact. On November 4th, however, the Politburo changed its mind and the Soviet Army crushed the revolt. The Revolution of 1856 was the first threat to Soviet control.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2016\/11\/IMAG4369\/3622017247.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Parliament: The Warsaw Pact was created on May 14th, 1955 in response to Western Germany's integration into NATO. On October 23rd, 1956, university students protested in front of Parliament. While there was no leader at the beginning, the revolt caught fire across Hungary. By the end of October, the violence had almost come to an end and the Soviets agreed to let Hungary out of the Warsaw Pact. On November 4th, however, the Politburo changed its mind and the Soviet Army crushed the revolt. The Revolution of 1856 was the first threat to Soviet control.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/IMAG4374.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"V\u00edgsz\u00ednh\u00e1z (Comedy Theater of Budapest) was damaged in 1945 due to bomb shells. It was repaired and opened six years later with the name Theatre of the People&#039;s Army. In 1960, it regained its original name.\" data-attachment-id=\"27\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"V\u00edgsz\u00ednh\u00e1z (Comedy Theater of Budapest) was damaged in 1945 due to bomb shells. It was repaired and opened s